# ── Build artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benchmark fixtures under plugins/rust-studio/benchmarks/ are source-only:
# nothing in this repo is meant to be compiled into the tree.
target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta

# Output of the studio's own tooling, when the plugin is dogfooded on this repo.
# cargo-mutants and cargo-fuzz write these; /mutants and /fuzz both expect them ignored.
mutants.out/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/corpus/

# ── Studio / agent runtime state ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-agent scratch memory the host writes into a project tree. Agent state, not
# plugin content — it must never ship in the distribution. Unanchored: the host writes
# it next to whatever tree the session is rooted in, including inside plugins/.
**/.claude/agent-memory/

# Host-local settings: machine-specific paths, permissions, claudeMdExcludes.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# Skill output written into the working project (`/research`, `/spec`, `/tech-debt`,
# progress logs). Scratch by design: anything durable gets promoted into docs/adr/,
# which is how the 2026-09 research survived its own autopilot run (ADR 0001).
.rust-studio/

# `claude plugin eval` scores — regenerated per run, and model-dependent.
plugins/rust-studio/evals/results/

# Autopilot working directory: one build run's brief, manifest, spec, tickets, live
# dashboard and resume state. Local by design — it dies with the run that produced it,
# and anything durable is promoted into docs/adr/ instead (ADR 0001). Untracked in
# 0.51.0; the files stay on disk, so "продолжи автопилот" still resumes.
.autopilot/

# ── Local caches and one-off backups ──────────────────────────────────────────
.build/
.fastembed_cache/
.serena/
plugins/.rust-studio.backup-pre-memory-unify/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Toolchain / editor / OS junk ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Merge/rebase leftovers — /merge-conflicts and /resolve-pr both produce these.
*.orig
*.rej
